message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it as
  below. This entry is anonymized for double-blind review; it will be
  updated with full author information upon acceptance.
title: >-
  The Iterated-Logarithm Price of Post-Hoc Threshold Selection
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
repository-code: "<ANONYMIZED-CODE-LINK>"
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying an ICLR 2027 submission (under double-blind review)
  introducing a risk-coverage certificate that remains valid under post-hoc
  threshold selection, an iterated-logarithm lower bound showing this price
  is unavoidable, and a block-robust extension for correlated failures.
keywords:
  - selective prediction
  - conformal prediction
  - anytime-valid inference
  - risk control
  - post-hoc selection
  - confidence sequences
